course: dictionary
lesson: 5669
title: Lively
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The Mole feels lively underground.» Lively means full of energy, fun and activity. The Mole loves digging and his cosy home, so he feels full of life there. The Rat likes a breezy river bedroom and feels sleepy and shut in at Badger's house, so the opposite of lively is sleepy or dull.
explain: Lively can describe a person, an animal or a place. A lively puppy bounces and runs about. A lively crowd is busy and noisy. A lively discussion is one where people talk with energy and interest, and a lively debate is a friendly argument.
explain: Lively can also describe colours. Lively colours are bright and strong, so a lively red is much brighter than a pale pink. To choose the right meaning, check the context: is the thing full of energy, busy and noisy, or bright?
fact: Lively means full of energy, fun and activity.
fact: A lively place, party or discussion is busy, exciting and noisy.
fact: Lively colours are bright and strong.
fact: «Look lively» is a UK phrase that means hurry up.
fact: Lively is an adjective. Its other forms are livelier and liveliest.
exercise: «The Mole feels lively underground.» What does lively mean here? | Lost and afraid | Very cold and wet | *Full of energy and activity | Covered in leaves
exercise: «The party was ___ with music, games and dancing.» Which word fits the gap? | *lively | pale | empty | sleepy
exercise: Ella says «look lively» means look happy. What does it really mean in the UK? | Look at the sky | Smile at everyone | *Hurry up | Sit down and rest
test: «The bright, lively colours of the painting made the whole room glow.» What does lively describe? | Something cold and quiet | A loud sound | *Something bright and strong | Something sleepy
test: «The ___ puppy chased its ball across the lawn.» Which word fits the gap? | pale | sad | silent | *lively
exam: Which phrase means the same as lively in «a lively crowd»? | Dull and grey | *Busy and noisy | Tired and slow | Quiet and still
